<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Eletrobras shares sold at auction.</title>
<headline>Brazil Eletrobras shares sold at auction.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Development Bank's investment unit, BNDESPar, raised 46.2 million reais ($45.2 million) by auctioning 149.5 million Eletrobras common shares in the forward market, the Rio de Janeiro bourse said.</p>
<p>Brazilian brokerage Omega acquired 91 percent of the shares put up for sale, which accounted for 0.28 percent of Eletrobras voting stake, a bourse spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The remainder was acquired by brokerages Factorial, Celio Araujo, Agenda and Teka.  The average price was 309.5 reais per lot of 1,000 shares, she said.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 232 4411</p>
